From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:08:08 +0100
Subject: build: drop the Qt 5 support, which could no longer build

CMakeLists.txt fell back to Qt 5 and poppler-qt5 when Qt 6 was not
found, and several headers switched on USE_QT6, but the code uses the
Qt 6 Poppler API (std::unique_ptr from Document::load() and page(),
Page::textList() returning a std::vector) and QByteArrayView, so a Qt 5
build could not compile.  Require Qt 6 and poppler-qt6 (still found via
Poppler's CMake config, pkg-config, or a plain search, for Homebrew's
keg-only formulas), and remove the USE_QT6 switches and the
QT_VERSION checks left over from Qt 4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
